  "response": {
    "html": "<h1 data-chunk-id=\"14811b8e-f943-4f2c-94c0-856af5ab6c82\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;border-bottom:3px solid #0d47a1;padding-bottom:6px\">Nebula Drift - Narrative</h1>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"75656251-4584-456b-b802-bc8ba4ca590d\" style=\"background-color:#e3f2fd;border-left:4px solid #1565c0;padding:8px 10px;font-size:9pt;color:#37474f\">Vantage Nine Studios - internal - sub-document of the Nebula Drift GDD.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"89eabd38-3321-477a-aac3-12b844380312\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Premise</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"27fc4de0-e399-44a5-94af-b0543cf67cab\">The Drift Belt was a shipyard until it was not. Nobody agrees on what\nhappened and the only person still transmitting has a reason to lie.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"d46afee4-4c8c-4006-8122-87e6e7f05c3a\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Act I - Salvage</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"8cb39544-16a0-4e81-8023-ba863a75ca78\">The player learns to move. Vex, on the channel, is helpful and slightly too\nwell informed about a place she claims never to have visited.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"5be45a25-a27f-4f10-8497-1adfb4695f43\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Act II - The Cartographer</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"619f8e14-89c8-4ad2-b074-966b56977ec3\">The wreck has been mapped before. The player starts finding the map, and it\nis annotated in Vex's hand.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"277c44a6-12b1-4e42-b50e-11358ef80ca9\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Act III - Drift</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"965e7752-ae50-4b4a-a37c-c371b4fff131\">The player can leave or finish the map. Both endings are short; neither is\nthe \"good\" one.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"247cc9eb-98dd-4530-b047-d1f7540bd931\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Characters</h2>\n<table data-chunk-id=\"ec838606-c311-4f2d-82de-bd78ef27a5d5\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #37474f;font-family:Inter , Calibri , Arial , sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"><thead><tr>\n<th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Character</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Role</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Voice</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">The Salvager</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Player</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Silent. Reads as competent, not heroic.</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Vex</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Voice on the channel</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Warm, funny, unreliable.</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">The Cartographer</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Antagonist, absent</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Never speaks. Only annotations.</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>",
